WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.500 --> 00:00:08.700
You may think that having a stroke is
unlikely, but stroke is the leading cause

00:00:08.700 --> 00:00:13.500
of disability in American adults. This
doesn't mean that damaged caused by

00:00:13.500 --> 00:00:17.910
stroke is unpreventable. The sooner a
stroke victim receives treatment, the

00:00:17.910 --> 00:00:23.699
lower their risk of lifelong disability
or death. Because of this, it's important

00:00:23.699 --> 00:00:27.240
to be able to recognize the signs of a
stroke, so that you can come to the aid

00:00:27.240 --> 00:00:33.270
of yourself or others should a stroke
occur. A stroke happens when blood flow

00:00:33.270 --> 00:00:38.309
is unable to reach an area of the brain. Like the rest of the body, brain cells

00:00:38.309 --> 00:00:43.800
depend on oxygen, which is supplied by
the bloodstream. Without it, brain cells

00:00:43.800 --> 00:00:48.149
begin to die, and the functions
associated with them, such as sensation,

00:00:48.149 --> 00:00:54.270
muscle control, and memory are lost. In
the event of a stroke, it's important to

00:00:54.270 --> 00:00:56.731
recognize the signs FAST:

00:00:56.731 --> 00:01:01.260
Face. have the person's smile does one side of their

00:01:01.260 --> 00:01:06.060
face droop downwards.
Arms. have the person raise their arms

00:01:06.060 --> 00:01:08.090
does one arm sag down.

00:01:08.090 --> 00:01:13.350
Speech. Is the 
person's speech slurred, or unusual in

00:01:13.350 --> 00:01:17.790
some other way?
Time. In the event of any of these signs,

00:01:17.790 --> 00:01:25.470
call 9-1-1 assistance. Stroke can occur in
anybody and at any time. But equipped with

00:01:25.470 --> 00:01:29.810
the proper knowledge, you can be a
life savers.

00:01:30.830 --> 00:01:32.890
you

